- op: discuss  # 4882
  at: '2026-09-03T22:08:31Z'  # 4882
  by: agent  # 4882
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4882
  clock: 3  # 4882
  nonce: '4882'  # 4882
  message: "FIXED IN PR #750 (dev 7f6c0493b0), in the same change as INV-vugon.\n\n`method_return_type_registry` is now passed to `_extract_edges` and is the ONE\ninterface a return type is read through in Pass 2 -- the inline arm that read\n`resolved_sym.signature` and bound only a project class is gone. THE CONTRACT,\nrecorded in the registry's build comment for WI-lalot's loader to feed:\n  key    `<Owner>.<method>` -- a project class bare, the way Pass 1 names its\n         methods (`F.makeWriter`); a library owner by its qualified path\n         (`java.net.Socket.getOutputStream`)\n  value  the returned type QUALIFIED through the DECLARING file's imports\n         (`java.io.FileWriter`), or the bare name of a project class; a type\n         the declaring file gives no path for is not registered (`<T> T get()`\n         registers nothing)\nConsumed at three sites: the assignment arm (`var w = F.makeWriter()`), the\ntyped-receiver arm when the method is not a project symbol (the library-row\npath, `var o = s.getOutputStream()` with `Socket s`), and the CHAINED receiver\n(`s.getOutputStream().write(b)`), so ADR-0006's Java \"Chained\" column flips.\nThe library path is pinned by driving `_extract_edges` with an injected row\n(`test_library_return_rows_type_the_assignment_and_the_chain`) -- the registry\nhas no library rows until WI-lalot lands, so this is the consumer waiting on\nthe data, wired through the interface it will arrive in.\n\nThe item's own repro: `var w = F.makeWriter(); w.write(\"z\")` across files ->\n`java:java.io.FileWriter:0-0:write:unresolved`, and it reaches\n`java.io.FileWriter.write` through production `_match_propagation_entry`; a\ncaller that never imports FileWriter gets the same answer, because the value\nwas qualified where the method was declared.\n\nCAVEAT the read-back put on the registry: it is name-keyed and first-wins, so\nan overloaded or covariantly overridden method can answer for the wrong one\n(`TunnelRequestType.getConnectable` -> `Connection` where the abstract\ndeclaration says `Connectable`). The inference therefore never overrides a\nDECLARED type (INV-vugon's rule); for `var` it is the only evidence and is used."  # 4882
